   "line": 7,
   "text": "Now each click launches its own copy of h. Linearity scales it by the click's size. Time-invariance starts it as many samples late as its click. Add the copies, sample by sample, and out comes the echo: five samples, starting at two thousand, peaking at point three two. [surprise-oh] One click just predicted the echo of a word you never sent.",
